rtant: Strongly prefer a more novel groundbreaking idea. We are interested in true novelty which would be interesting to domain experts. Examples of not truly novel ideas: - combinations of existing well known mechanisms have limited novelty and is not groundbreaking. - suggesting that an already known mechanism is the main mechanism has limited novelty. - suggesting that influence is direct when the influence is already known has limited novelty. - suggesting a known mechanism and testing it in a new way has limited novelty.

